<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-O6>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-O6" ;
  triage:title "attach_timeline is not idempotent: a second call swaps the bridge's sink to a new writer and spawns a second flush thread while the first OnceLock-held writer/counters remain live" ;
  triage:description "fenix-C architecture/boundaries review (01M1S751VVM0K4C7ZW6YDPC7BQ, their F6). attach_timeline (crates/atm-observability/src/tracing_bridge.rs) is not idempotent: a second call would swap the bridge's sink to a new writer and spawn a second flush thread while leaving the first OnceLock-held writer/counters live, so the original sink would silently stop being flushed on cadence. Not reachable today (called exactly once in production), but nothing guards against a future second call introducing a silent data-loss regression. Consistent with fenix-A's minor #7 (related OnceLock/flush-thread observations, same file, same design shape -- see also AW-READY-N6 bundle and AW-READY-M8 bundle item (c)). Fix: guard attach_timeline with an explicit already-attached check that errors loudly (or is a documented no-op) rather than silently reassigning the sink." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary-contract" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T16:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AW1 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T16:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
